  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">DKIM <xref target="RFC6376" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6376"/> signs email messages by creating hashes of selected
message header fields and body and signing the header hash with a
digital signature.  Message recipients fetch the signature
verification key from the DNS.  The defining documents specify a
single signing algorithm, RSA <xref target="RFC3447" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3447"/> (which has since been
obsoleted by <xref target="RFC8017" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC8017"/>).</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">This document adds a new, stronger signing algorithm, Edwards-Curve
Digital Signature Algorithm, using the Curve25519 curve (Ed25519),
which has much shorter keys than RSA for similar levels of security.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="conventions-used-in-this-document" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-conventions-used-in-this-document">Conventions Used in This Document</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">The key words &quot;<bcp14>MUST</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>REQUIRED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL NOT</bcp14>&quot;,
&quot;<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHOULD NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>RECOMMENDED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>NOT RECOMMENDED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MAY</bcp14>&quot;, and
&quot;<bcp14>OPTIONAL</bcp14>&quot; in this document are to be interpreted as described in
BCP 14 <xref target="RFC2119" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2119"/> <xref target="RFC8174" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC8174"/> when, and only when, they appear in all
capitals, as shown here.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-2">Syntax descriptions use Augmented BNF (ABNF) <xref target="RFC5234" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5234"/>.  The ABNF
tokens sig-a-tag-k and key-k-tag-type are imported from <xref target="RFC6376" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6376"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="ed25519-sha256-signing-algorithm" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3">
      <name slugifiedName="name-ed25519-sha256-signing-algorithm">Ed25519-SHA256 Signing Algorithm</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">The Ed25519-SHA256 signing algorithm computes a message hash as
defined in <xref target="RFC6376" section="3" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6376#section-3" derivedContent="RFC6376"/> using SHA-256 <xref target="FIPS-180-4-2015" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="FIPS-180-4-2015"/> as
the hash-alg.  It signs the hash with the PureEdDSA variant Ed25519,
as defined in RFC 8032, Section 5.1 <xref target="RFC8032" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC8032"/>.  Example keys and
signatures in <xref target="section-appendix.a" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Appendix A"/> are based on the test vectors in RFC 8032,
Section 7.1 <xref target="RFC8032" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC8032"/>.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-2">The DNS record for the verification public key has a &quot;k=ed25519&quot; tag
to indicate that the key is an Ed25519 rather than an RSA key.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-3">This is an additional DKIM signature algorithm added to <xref target="RFC6376" section="3.3" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6376#section-3.3" derivedContent="RFC6376"/> as envisioned in Section 3.3.4 of that document.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-4">Note: since Ed25519 public keys are 256 bits long, the base64-encoded
key is only 44 octets, so DNS key record data will generally fit in a
single 255-byte TXT string and work even with DNS provisioning
software that doesn't handle multistring TXT records.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="signature-and-key-syntax" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4">
      <name slugifiedName="name-signature-and-key-syntax">Signature and Key Syntax</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">The syntax of DKIM signatures and DKIM keys are updated as follows.</t>
      <section anchor="signature-syntax" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4.1">
        <name slugifiedName="name-signature-syntax">Signature Syntax</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.1-1">The syntax of DKIM algorithm tags in <xref target="RFC6376" section="3.5" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6376#section-3.5" derivedContent="RFC6376"/> is
updated by adding this rule to the existing rule for sig-a-tag-k:</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.1-2">ABNF:</t>
        <sourcecode type="abnf" markers="false" pn="section-4.1-3"><![CDATA[
sig-a-tag-k =/ "ed25519"
]]></sourcecode>
      </section>
      <section anchor="key-syntax" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4.2">
        <name slugifiedName="name-key-syntax">Key Syntax</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2-1">The syntax of DKIM key tags in <xref target="RFC6376" section="3.6.1" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6376#section-3.6.1" derivedContent="RFC6376"/> is updated
by adding this rule to the existing rule for key-k-tag-type:</t>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2-2">ABNF:</t>
        <sourcecode type="abnf" markers="false" pn="section-4.2-3"><![CDATA[
key-k-tag-type  =/ "ed25519"
]]></sourcecode>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2-4">The p= value in the key record is the Ed25519 public key encoded in
base64.  Since the key is 256 bits long, the base64 text is 44 octets
long.  See <xref target="section-a.2" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Appendix A.2"/> for a sample key record using the public key
in <xref target="RFC8032" section="7.1" format="default" sectionFormat="comma" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8032#section-7.1" derivedContent="RFC8032"/>, Test 1.</t>
      </section>
    </section>
    <section anchor="choice-and-strength-of-keys-and-algorithms" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-5">
      <name slugifiedName="name-choice-and-strength-of-keys-and-algorithms">Choice and Strength of Keys and Algorithms</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-1"><xref target="RFC6376" section="3.3" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6376#section-3.3" derivedContent="RFC6376"/> describes DKIM's hash and signature
algorithms.  It is updated as follows:</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-2">Signers <bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14> implement and verifiers <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> implement the
Ed25519-SHA256 algorithm.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="transition-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-6">
      <name slugifiedName="name-transition-considerations">Transition Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-6-1">For backward compatibility, signers can add multiple signatures that
use old and new signing algorithms.  Since there can only be a single
key record in the DNS for each selector, the signatures have to use
different selectors, although they can use the same d= and i=
identifiers.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-6-2">The example message in <xref target="section-appendix.a" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="Appendix A"/> has two signatures with the same d=
and i= identifiers but different a= algorithms and s= selectors.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-7">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-7-1">All of the security advice in <xref target="RFC6376" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6376"/> continues to apply, except
that the security advice about Ed25519 in <xref target="RFC8032" section="8" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedLink="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8032#section-8" derivedContent="RFC8032"/>
supplants the advice about RSA threats.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-8">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-considerations">IANA Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-8-1">IANA has updated a registry as follows.</t>
      <section anchor="dkim-key-type-registry" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-8.1">
        <name slugifiedName="name-dkim-key-type-registry">&quot;DKIM Key Type&quot; Registry</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-8.1-1">The following value has been added to the &quot;DKIM Key Type&quot; registry:</t>
        <table anchor="table-1" align="center" pn="table-1">
          <name slugifiedName="name-value-added-to-the-dkim-key-type-registry">Value Added to the &quot;DKIM Key Type&quot; Registry</name>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th align="center" colspan="1" rowspan="1">TYPE</th>
              <th align="center" colspan="1" rowspan="1">REFERENCE</th>
              <th align="center" colspan="1" rowspan="1">STATUS</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">ed25519</td>
              <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><xref target="RFC8032" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC8032"/></td>
              <td align="left" colspan="1" rowspan="1">active</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>
    </section>
  </middle>
